<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomás Regalado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomás Regalado was a Salvadoran general who seized power in November 1898 and was president of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> until 1903. His coup withdrew El Salvador from the Greater Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, which then dissolved. He was killed in 1906 while leading Salvadoran troops in a war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>.</p></div>
